and we call it  the ipad  apple's ipads have been using lcd  technology ever since the original ipad  and even the new mini led ipad pro  models are still technically using lcd  panels so it should make us wonder why  apple has refused to switch to oled over  the years and when they'll actually be  making the switch so in this video i'm  not only going to answer those questions  but i'm going to delve into the latest  rumors of how apple is finishing out the  releases of their final lcd and mini led  ipad pro models while setting in stone  their master plan for switching to oled  displays across their entire ipad lineup  and i actually think that this is quite  genius so without further ado let's  begin with some brand new rumors we got  over the weekend concerning apple's  upcoming ipad air 5 refresh coming this  spring in either march or april  according to mack otakara the new air  will be getting the a15 bionic chip the  12 megapixel ultra wide selfie camera  with center stage support optional 5g  and quad led true tone flash which is  all very obvious because those are the  features that the ipad mini 6 recently  was upgraded with so it only makes sense  for the ipad air to get them as well  especially since the current air is more  expensive than the mini now apart from  those obvious updates makatakara says  that we could expect the new ipad air to  finally get an upgrade to feature quad  speakers instead of the current dual  speaker situation on the ipad air 4  which is actually pretty weird because  it has four speaker grilles but only two  of them have speakers behind them so it  makes sense for the new one to use all  four grilles but other than that they  also mentioned that the ipad air could  be getting the same dual camera setup as  the current ipad pro models have and  maybe even the lidar scanner and all of  this would actually make sense because  apple has a history of bringing their  best technology to the ipad pro first  and then slowly trickling those features  down to the rest of the ipads starting  with the ipad air then the mini and then  finally to the budget ipad like for  example dylan dkt on twitter just  confirmed that the upcoming 10th gen  budget ipad will have a very minimal  update later this year with optional 5g  connectivity and a new a14 chip with it  being the last model before the big  redesign planned for next year but the  very interesting leaks we gotta get into  are the ones for the 2022 ipad pro  models first of all we're expecting both  the 11 and 12.9 inch models to get the  new m2 chip which will debut in the  redesigned macbook air and that will  obviously be much faster than the a15  chip that's going into the upcoming ipad  air 5. but on top of that we're also  expecting apple to give us a huge design  change by adding max safe wireless  charging to the back of the new ipad pro  models potentially within a new larger  apple glass logo which i recently made a  video on and probably even a new magsafe  magic keyboard case and going further we  also got some rumors of apple upgrading  the camera system to match the triple  camera setup we currently have on the  iphone 13 pro lineup which is probably  why the new air is getting the old dual  camera design and then the final rumor  that makes total sense to me is that the  11 inch ipad pro would now finally get  the mini led display that you can  currently only get on the 12.9 inch  model and with that i personally expect  the base price to jump up to 899 dollars  instead of the current 799 price and  then with that said this finally brings  us to apple's oled master plan and how  they could kick-start the transition and  brace yourselves because this is about  to get interesting but first i need to  quickly explain why apple has been  avoiding oled for so long first of all  oled has always been pretty expensive  and there used to be a lot of problems  with display burn-in after a few years  and other issues like oled displays just  not being that bright but now all the  technology has been improving and things  like color accuracy display angles color  shift and burn-in are drastically  improved compared to previous  generations so it seems like apple might  finally be ready to make the switch so  let's get into how they're gonna do this  the rumors of the very first oled ipad  began back in march of 2021 with digi  times claiming that an oled 10.9 inch  ipad would come in early 2022  which we know right now is not happening  anymore but the interesting point is  that they said it'll have a 10.9 inch  display which can only be the ipad air  since the pro models start at 11 inches  now in the same month of march ming chi  quo came out and confirmed that the ipad  air would adopt oled in 2022  with mini led remaining exclusive to the  ipad pro models because of the  advantages of higher brightness and then  in june the elec basically said the same  thing a new ipad air with oled in 2022  but then finally in july the very  reliable ross young came out and said  that the first 10.9 inch oled ipad would  not be coming until 2023  so it looks like it's been delayed for  sure so with all that said i can agree  that it makes total sense for the ipad  air to get an oled display next year and  since the ipad air is usually on a one  to one and a half year update cycle i  expect this oled ipad air to be released  in the fall of 2023 but then everything  got a little bit more confusing because  we also got some recent reports of a new  oled display for apple's ipad pro models  which could go from 120 hertz down to 10  hertz refresh rate just like the new  iphone 13 pro models can and over the  past week the elec has again confirmed  that this new panel would be launching  in 2024  using samsung display as the  manufacturer and just yesterday et news  reported that lg is also preparing to  supply oled panels for the ipad by 2024  and what makes all of this really  confusing is that we have conflicting  release dates for conflicting ipad  models but i think that i've finally  figured everything out and i figured out  how apple could make this transition as  smooth as possible my prediction is that  in the fall of 2023  apple's gonna release a new ipad air  with an oled display that will have much  better contrast levels compared to the  current lcd models however it will not  be better than the mini led ipad pro  models because the oled panel on the  ipad air is going to be limited to  around 500 to 600 nits of brightness as  well as only having a 60hz refresh rate  but either way the oled panel is still  going to be a nice upgrade over the  current lcd air so it's going to justify  a price increase but then around half a  year later in the spring of 2024 i  expect apple to release a new 12.9 inch  ipad pro model with an even better oled  panel because that's actually what  digitimes reported on way back in march  of last year and if you're wondering  what i mean by an even better oled panel  this brings us to a report from the  elect back in november where they claim  that the future ipad pro and macbook pro  models would feature ultra bright double  stack oled displays so they'll  essentially have two of the same display  panel stacked on top of each other to  literally double the brightness so that  the ipad pro models will still support  real hdr with at least a thousand or  maybe 1200 nits of brightness and the  even bigger benefit is that the oled  technology would mean that the current  display blooming issues with the mini  led displays would completely go away  while also enabling them to support  hertz promotion like the current models  have so it would basically create the  ultimate oled display with no  compromises and that would of course  warrant a price increase as it would be  a much better display compared to the  ipad air model which will only have a  single oled panel limited in brightness  and refresh rate and then sometime in  2025 i expect the 11 inch ipad pro model  to get updated with that same new oled  display at a base price of 999  and then the ipad mini will adopt the  lower end oled display also probably in  2025 and then with that said probably a  full year after that sometime in 2026  the budget ipad will finally get the  oled display and then that's how i  expect apple's full oled ipad transition  to take place finishing up completely  within around three years time which  isn't bad at all so there you guys go  that's my take on apple's oled master  plan transition and if you totally  disagree with my thoughts on how apple  will implement oled on these ipads then  go ahead and comment down below but if  you enjoyed the video tap the like  button and click the circle above to  subscribe for more videos like this one  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]

